+### §check-fails-closed — a failing command aborts the check with a non-zero exit
+- Since: 2026-10-22. Replaces §check-fails-open (2026-09-11), which the maintainer explicitly overrode.
+- Decision: `set -euo pipefail`. Any failing command aborts the check with a non-zero exit. Large staged files still
+  only produce a warning. A test whose false result is not an error is written as `if …; then …; fi`, not
+  `test && cmd`, because a false test as the loop's last command would abort the check.
+- Forbidden: removing `-e` (`set -e` / `set -o errexit`).
+- Rejected: fail-open (`set -uo pipefail` without `-e`, always `exit 0`), the 2026-09-11 decision.
+- Reason: the maintainer overrode §check-fails-open on 2026-10-22 so that any failing command aborts the check
+  with a non-zero exit. History: with `set -e`, a `wc` failure on a staged-then-deleted file once blocked every commit
+  for a day (2026-09-10). The `[ -f "$f" ] || continue` guard now skips such files before `wc` runs.
